      "body": "Signed-off-by: Elvir Crncevic <elvircrn@gmail.com>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nWhile profiling, I ran into an instance of freakishly long `ncclDevKernel_AllGather_RING_LL(ncclDevKernelArgsStorage<4096ul>)` and `ncclDevKernel_ReduceScatter_Sum_bf16_RING_LL(ncclDevKernelArgsStorage<4096ul>)` seemingly caused by or causing cudagraph breakage.\r\n\r\nReproduction steps:\r\n\r\n```\r\nVLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=1 VLLM_HUMMING_MOE_GEMM_TYPE=indexed PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True VLLM_HUMMING_INPUT_QUANT_CONFIG='{\"dtype\":\"float8e4m3\",\"group_size\":128}' vllm serve mgoin/Kimi-K3-pruned75   --port 8000   --trust-remote-code   --max-model-len auto   --disable-access-log-for-endpoints=/health,/metrics   --enable-expert-parallel   --tensor-parallel-size 4   --data-parallel-size 2    --all2all-backend deepep_v2   --language-model-only   --attention-backend FLASHMLA   --moe-backend humming   --disable-custom-all-reduce   --no-enable-flashinfer-autotune   --enable-auto-tool-choice   --tool-call-parser kimi_k3   --profiler-config '{\"profiler\":\"torch\",\"torch_profiler_dir\":\"/var/cache/vllm/profile\",\"torch_profiler_record_shapes\":false,\"torch_profiler_with_memory\":false,\"max_iterations\":5,\"torch_profiler_with_stack\":false}' --max-num-batched-tokens 512                   --max-num-seqs 128\r\n```\r\n\r\nLoad:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlm_eval --model local-chat-completions   --model_args \"model=mgoin/Kimi-K3-pruned75,base_url=http://localhost:8000/v1/chat/completions,num_concurrent=8\"   --tasks gsm8k   --num_fewshot 7   --apply_chat_template   --gen_kwargs \"temperature=0,do_sample=False\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<img width=\"3006\" height=\"1556\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/02cb7b02-6f60-4f49-b35d-35726ce47e02\" />\r\n\r\nProfiler [artifact](https://elvircrn.github.io/tv/?gist=f20c4a6bd85de1d8c53cb37bda0b8eae).\r\n\r\nI am uncertain if this PR fixed the root cause of the issue.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [ ] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [ ] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
